<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Paperlane Studio</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f6efe4;
      --paper: #fffaf2;
      --paper-soft: #f1e6d7;
      --ink: #2f251d;
      --muted: #6c5d50;
      --line: #d8c7b1;
      --accent: #b96f39;
      --accent-soft: #fae1ca;
      --shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(77, 49, 25, 0.08);
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: "Palatino Linotype", "Book Antiqua", serif;
      color: var(--ink);
      background:
        linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.4), rgba(255,255,255,0)),
        var(--bg);
    }
    a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    .shell { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
    .topbar {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 10;
      backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
      background: rgba(246, 239, 228, 0.88);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(216, 199, 177, 0.8);
    }
    .topbar-inner,
    .footer-box {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 18px 0;
    }
    .brand {
      font-size: 22px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    }
    .brand span { color: var(--accent); }
    .nav, .footer-nav {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 18px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(280px, 0.82fr);
      gap: 22px;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 70px 0 24px;
    }
    .chip {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 32px;
      padding: 0 12px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 18px 0 16px;
      font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 76px);
      line-height: 0.98;
    }
    .lead {
      max-width: 640px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.8;
      margin: 0 0 24px;
    }
    .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }
    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      padding: 0 16px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--paper);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .button.primary {
      border-color: var(--accent);
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #fff7f0;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .card, .panel, .footer-box {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 24px;
      background: rgba(255, 250, 242, 0.9);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    .panel { padding: 22px; }
    .mini-list {
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 16px;
    }
    .mini-item {
      padding: 12px 14px;
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--paper-soft);
    }
    section { padding: 22px 0; }
    .section-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: end;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .section-head h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    }
    .section-head p,
    .card p,
    .footer-box p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }
    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .card { padding: 20px; }
    .card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 21px;
    }
    .notes { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
    .note {
      padding-top: 12px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .note:first-child { padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
    .footer-wrap { padding: 26px 0 60px; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .hero, .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .topbar-inner, .section-head, .footer-box { display: block; }
      .nav, .footer-nav { margin-top: 14px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="shell topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">Paperlane <span>Studio</span></a>
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#services">Services</a>
        <a href="#journal">Journal</a>
        <a href="#methods">Methods</a>
        <a href="#footer">About</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="top" class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="chip">Editorial delivery and quiet web operations</span>
        <h1>Publishing surfaces with a calmer operational rhythm.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Paperlane Studio supports editorial teams, small networks, and independent
          programs that need durable web delivery, modest support overhead, and a refined public front.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="#services">Our services</a>
          <a class="button" href="#journal">Recent notes</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="panel">
        <strong>Studio bulletin</strong>
        <p>Current intake remains limited to structured refresh work, archive-focused migrations, and recurring maintenance support.</p>
        <div class="mini-list">
          <div class="mini-item">Quarterly surface reviews</div>
          <div class="mini-item">Managed rollout windows</div>
          <div class="mini-item">Minimal public change noise</div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="services">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Services</h2>
        <p>Public-facing copy stays intentionally broad, but the layout feels like a real boutique studio rather than a placeholder page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Publishing support</h3>
          <p>Clean delivery surfaces for controlled releases, evergreen notices, and low-friction archive pages.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Access planning</h3>
          <p>Support for gated paths, stable retrieval surfaces, and scheduled content maintenance.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Site continuity</h3>
          <p>Light operational review to keep editorial publishing stable through certificate and routing changes.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="journal">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Studio journal</h2>
        <p>A small set of dated notes makes the site feel maintained without requiring a real CMS or multiple pages.</p>
      </div>
      <article class="card notes">
        <div class="note">
          <strong>April note</strong>
          <p>Spring review windows are focused on archive reliability and simplified publication handoffs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          <strong>March note</strong>
          <p>We consolidated update notices into a shorter release format for returning operators.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          <strong>February note</strong>
          <p>Fallback publishing surfaces were refreshed for smaller distribution footprints.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section id="methods">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Working methods</h2>
        <p>Structured maintenance, short review loops, and simple public-facing language.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p>Paperlane prefers small, predictable changes over large redesign cycles. That approach keeps delivery steady and makes the public site read like a live studio property.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <div id="footer" class="footer-wrap shell">
    <div class="footer-box">
      <div>
        <strong>Paperlane Studio</strong>
        <p>Independent publishing support for refined, low-maintenance digital delivery.</p>
      </div>
      <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="#top">Top</a>
        <a href="#services">Services</a>
        <a href="#journal">Journal</a>
        <a href="#methods">Methods</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
